🎯 One-line explanation for your Lead

You can explain the approach like this:

“For Phase 1, I propose using Playwright against the WebSphere Admin Console to validate critical availability — WebSphere servers/JVMs, Web Server, Nodes, Clusters, critical Applications and their deployment mapping. The objective is to quickly identify basic availability or deployment issues before they impact testing or users. Once Phase 1 is stable, Phase 2 can extend into JVM runtime, thread pools, JDBC, response time, logs, configuration and dependency health checks.”

💡 The key philosophy

Phase 1 = “Is everything required UP?”

Phase 2 = “Is everything UP and behaving normally?”

That distinction will make your proposal very easy for your lead to understand.
